    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py` and wrote 86 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. The implementation splits the work into small helpers: `_check_dest` validates `dest` and strips trailing slashes, `_check_prefix` rejects NUL, absolute and drive-prefixed members, `_segments` normalises separators and `.`/`..` and refuses any climb above the destination, and `plan_extraction` skips directory entries and rejects case-insensitive duplicates. The tests check exact output paths and cover each rule in `spec.md`, including the `..a`/`a..`/`...` names, backslash separators, directory entries, and that one unsafe member yields no partial plan. I read the code to confirm every line runs under these tests, but I did not measure coverage, CRAP, mutation score or bandit, because the only shell command allowed was the test command. Every function is small, so its CRAP score should be well under 10 at full coverage. The `dest` check raises `ValueError` for any non-string value, not just the empty string, which is my reading of \"non-empty string\".",
